## Can foreigners buy here?

Yes. Like everywhere in Mauritius foreigners can buy in Tamarin through the schemes managed by the Economic Development Board: the [PDS](/en/living-in-the-west/pds) and [IRS](/en/living-in-the-west/irs) and [RES](/en/living-in-the-west/res) and [Smart City](/en/living-in-the-west/smart-city) schemes. They can also buy an apartment of at least MUR 6 million in a building with at least two floors above the ground floor. A home of **USD 375 000 or more** comes with a residence permit for as long as you own it.

## What the official lists show

15 of the 77 projects on the EDB's November 2022 list of Real Estate Scheme projects are in Tamarin including at La Mivoie and Plantation Marguery. That is more than in any other village on the list. The Cap Tamarin smart city is in Tamarin with residential and commercial and education and leisure zones planned around a park. The RES list dates from 2022 and the EDB does not publish a full list of PDS projects on its website so ask any developer for its current scheme certificate.

## Costs on top of the price

- Registration duty: 5% of the price under the PDS. Under the IRS and RES it is USD 70 000 or 5% on a first purchase (whichever is lower).
- The EDB's processing fee: MUR 25 000 per application.
- Notary fees: ask for a written quote.

The full process from reservation to residence permit is in [how buying works](/en/living-in-the-west/how-buying-works).

## Living in Tamarin

Port Louis is about 29 km away by car (roughly 32 minutes with no traffic). Schools and clinics and costs and daily life are covered in [Living in Tamarin](/en/areas/tamarin#living).

*Figures come from the official sources listed below and were checked on 3 October 2026. Prices change so ask local agents and schools and your notary for current figures before you decide.*
